	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/prism/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="How the world is lit. Classic: the game's own light. PRISM Rebaked: light baked on this computer (sun, sky, lamps, bounces). PRISM Path Traced: every light traced each frame. The PRISM lightings need a graphics card that traces rays.|The rows below follow the lighting chosen."/>
		<string text="Classic's shadows, smooth lighting, dynamic lights and ambient occlusion, and PRISM's extras on Classic's light: smoother lightmaps, highlights, reflections and sun shadows."/>
		<string text="How PRISM Rebaked composes its frame and lights characters and vehicles, their shadows, and the dynamic lights."/>
		<string text="Path Traced's profile and denoiser (PRISM's or DLSS Ray Reconstruction), and the moving lights: plasma, needles, blasts and shield flares."/>
		<string text="The traced features of the lighting chosen: Classic's ray traced shadows and light, and the shapes every lighting traces (models, cutouts)."/>
		<string text="The PRISM lightings' exposure and tone curve, and the bloom and tone grade of every lighting."/>
		<string text="Draws the 3D view smaller and brings it to the screen's resolution with FSR 3.1 or DLSS: faster. The upscaler and how much of the resolution it starts from."/>
		<string text="The levels' light, baked on this computer on the main menu before you play, which both PRISM lightings read: its quality, the sky's light, and each level's bake."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="The materials packs and mods give surfaces, and the sharper textures mods ship, with how much of the graphics card they take."/>
		<string text="The remodelled characters, weapons and vehicles mods ship, and how the sharper assets are read in without popping."/>
		<string text="The level remodelled from the data folder, and under the PRISM lightings the HQ ground, footprints and PRISM's water."/>
	</strings>
</menus>
